Initial TT96 typecheck exited 2: src/lib/programmer.ts used three BigInt literals, but the repository TypeScript target is below ES2020 (TS2737). The implementation was changed to BigInt(0), without changing the target; a fresh check is required. An earlier unit-test import caught every import error and silently fell back to the old evaluator. The test was repaired to fall back only when the module is absent, and the Node strip-types-incompatible constructor parameter properties were replaced with explicit fields. See tt96-programmer-first-recheck.log and tt96-programmer-recheck.log.
